# A conformance transcript for HTTP mode (design section 5.1).
#
# One line per message. "> " is the body of a POST from bactrian to the agent
# and "< " a message in the JSON array the agent answers it with (the array of
# the "<" lines that follow, empty for "start" and "end"). Lines starting with
# "#" and blank lines are comments.
#
# Every POST has the method POST, "Content-Type: application/json", the header
# "X-Bactrian-Run" and the experiment's namespace header, both holding the run
# ID of the "start" message. The "start" message carries "env", the per-run
# environment a command agent would get as process variables. Its keys are in
# sorted order because decoding sorts the keys of a JSON object, and the test
# suite's round trip from decode to encode relies on that.
#
# The ">" lines are the bytes the agent driver writes for these messages. A
# real run builds its own messages from a scenario, includes the variables of
# all four providers, and the order of the keys of "env" is not part of the
# contract. An agent may answer with other key order or spacing: the test suite
# decodes it.

> {"v":1,"type":"start","run_id":"run-1","scenario":"weather","variant":"baseline","sim_now":"2026-03-01T09:00:00Z","state_dir":"/work/.bactrian/runs/run-1/state","env":{"BACTRIAN_RUN_ID":"run-1","BACTRIAN_STATE_DIR":"/work/.bactrian/runs/run-1/state","OPENAI_API_KEY":"bactrian-00000000000000000000000000000001","OPENAI_BASE_URL":"http://127.0.0.1:41000/r/00000000000000000000000000000001/openai/v1","SIM_NOW":"2026-03-01T09:00:00Z","TZ":"Europe/London"}}
> {"v":1,"type":"turn","turn":1,"content":"What is the weather in Paris?"}
< {"v":1,"type":"event","turn":1,"name":"tool","data":{"name":"get_weather","arguments":{"city":"Paris"}}}
< {"v":1,"type":"reply","turn":1,"content":"It is 18 degrees Celsius and cloudy in Paris."}
> {"v":1,"type":"turn","turn":2,"content":"And in Zürich? Say \"briefly\".\nThanks."}
< {"v":1,"type":"reply","turn":2,"content":"Cool, 9 degrees.\nLight rain."}
> {"v":1,"type":"turn","turn":3,"content":"Thanks"}
< {"v":1,"type":"reply","turn":3,"content":"You are welcome."}
> {"v":1,"type":"end"}
